@startuml
title UC12 - Level Up - Use Case Description

map "UC12 - Level Up" as UC12 {
  Name => Level Up
  ID => UC12
  Description => Pokemon gains experience after battle victory and levels up when EXP threshold is reached
  Actor => System (ExpService)
  Organizational Benefits => Core progression mechanic keeping players engaged through Pokemon growth
  Trigger => Player wins a battle (UC2, UC14, UC15, UC16) and EXP is awarded
  Preconditions => 1. Player has won a battle \n 2. Participating Pokemon earned enough EXP to level up \n 3. Pokemon is not at maximum level
  Postconditions => 1. Pokemon level increased \n 2. Stats recalculated \n 3. New moves or evolution checked
  Main Course => 1. System calculates EXP reward based on defeated Pokemon level \n 2. System distributes EXP to participating Pokemon \n 3. System checks if accumulated EXP exceeds level threshold \n 4. Pokemon level increases by 1 \n 5. System recalculates all stats (HP, Attack, Defense, Speed) \n 6. System checks for new move learning at current level \n 7. System checks evolution conditions \n 8. System displays level up notification with stat changes
  Alternate Courses => 1. New move available -> prompt to learn or skip \n 2. Move slots full (4 moves) -> prompt to replace existing \n 3. Evolution triggered -> transform Pokemon via WorldGenService \n 4. Player cancels evolution -> Pokemon stays in current form \n 5. Multiple level ups -> process each level sequentially
  Exceptions => 1. Pokemon at max level -> display max level message \n 2. Evolution data missing -> skip evolution, log warning
}

@enduml
